== Crystal 2 (X2) ==

A second quartz crystal resonator (X2) produces another reference clock which is synthesized by the PLL clock generator and routed to RDRAM. X2 is multiplied by 17<ref>On early boards using MX8330MC/MX9911MC, this multiplier requires FSEL to be tied high on X2's paired discrete synthesizer. On boards with MX8350, this is a fixed 17× multiplier regardless of NTSC/!PAL pin state.</ref> to produce RCLK,<ref>RCLK is distributed via Rambus Signaling Logic (RSL), a low-voltage swing interface, via the synthesizer's '''FSO''' pin. This is distinct from the Transistor-Transistor Logic (TTL) '''FSO/5''' pin used for VCLK. FSC output is also TTL-compatible.</ref> from which all non-AV system clocks are derived, including the MasterClock (MClock).<ref>See [[SysAD_Interface]].</ref>

All values in MHz:

