=== [[VR4300]] Clock Domains ===

The NUS-CPU itself generates clock domains using an integrated PLL, referenced to the MClock input. This clock architecture is described in the NEC VR4300 documentation:

* '''PClock''': Principal operating frequency; generated from MClock via PLL using DivMode configuration pins (sampled on cold reset). Frequency is divided by 4 in low-power mode.
* '''SClock''': Internal system interface clock; normally equal to MClock. Reduced in tandem with PClock in low-power mode.
* '''TClock''': Transmit clock output for external agents. Always equal to MasterClock regardless of DivMode setting.

{| class="wikitable" style="text-align:center"
|-
! DivMode (1:0) !! MClock : PClock !! MClock (MHz) !! PClock (MHz)
|-
| <code>0b00</code><ref>DivMode value <code>0b00</code> is marked RFU (Reserved for Future Use) in the VR4300 User's Manual. In the MTI R4300i documentation, this mode is indicated to use a 1:1 ratio.</ref> || 1 : 1 || 62.5 || 62.5
|-
| <code>0b01</code> || 1 : 1.5 || 62.5 || 93.75
|-
| <code>0b10</code> || 1 : 2 || 62.5 || 125
|-
| <code>0b11</code> || 1 : 3 || 62.5 || 187.5
|}

The [https://n64brew.dev/wiki/File:VR4300-Users-Manual.pdf VR4300 manual] also notes: "The maximum value of PClock is the same as the maximum internal operating frequency of each product regardless of the frequency ratio." The higher DivMode ratios exceed the nominal operating specification of an umodified N64 CPU.

